Package: epiLabR
Type: Package
Title: Educational Framework for Compartmental Epidemiological Modelling
Version: 0.3.0
Author: Vicente Castellar [aut, cre]
Authors@R: 
    person("Vicente", "Castellar",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "vic.sebastia@gmail.com")
Description: Tools for simulation of deterministic compartmental
    epidemiological models defined by systems of ordinary differential equations
    (ODEs). The package allows users to define custom epidemic models, simulate
    state trajectories over time, and explore model behaviour under different
    parameter settings. It includes implementations of classical compartmental
    models such susceptible-infectious-recovered (SIR) models, as well as related extensions. 
    An optional 'shiny' application is provided for interactive visualisation and 
    exploration of epidemic scenarios. The methodological framework is based on 
    Kermack and McKendrick (1927) <doi:10.1098/rspa.1927.0118>,
    Hethcote (2000) <doi:10.1137/S0036144500371907>, 
    Soetaert et al. (2010) <doi:10.18637/jss.v033.i09>, 
    Ma (2020) <doi:10.1016/j.idm.2019.12.009>.
